  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:shared.typing.given_fragment against lean:Correspondence/UniqueSharedTyping:given_fragment. given_fragment contains bidirectional expression, binding, statement, sequence and program typing, arbitrary-successor step/trace reflection and completion equivalence. The contextual embedClass assigns classType and given fields, embedType assigns given, and the operational embedding assigns unique. Consequently neither the struct guards nor immediately shared constructors affect the embedded Given fragment; unpacking is explicitly included. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:shared.typing.statements, unit:shared.typing.sequences, unit:shared.typing.patterns, unit:shared.typing.steps, unit:shared.typing.outcomes, unit:given.typing.statements, unit:shared.embedding, unit:shared.correspondence, unit:given.unpacking.",
